# Build-context filter for `docker build`: a container build works from source only, so generated
# output, editor state, and version-control metadata are kept out of the context. This is NOT
# .gitignore - several paths excluded below are deliberately tracked in Git.
#
# WARNING - never add a pattern that matches a build input: a root build or configuration manifest,
# the SDK pin, the editor-config file carrying the path-scoped analyzer exemption, or anything
# under src/ or tests/.
#
# Patterns match against the context root; the recursive **/ form catches an artifact at any depth.

## Build output - regenerated inside the SDK stage; must never leak in from the host
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
publish/
**/*.binlog

## Test and coverage output
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx
**/coverage*.*

## Version control and CI metadata (not needed to build the solution)
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

## Container definitions (inputs to `docker build` itself, not to the build inside it)
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

## IDE / editor state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/*.DotSettings.user

## Documentation (not an input to the build)
README.md
LICENSE

## OS noise - recursive form so a stray file is caught at any depth, root included
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*~
